# Repo Hygiene

## Track in git

- Source, tests, docs, CI workflows, `*.example` configs, Gradle lockfiles / version catalogs
- Agent process files (`AGENTS.md`, `BUILD_PLAN.md`, `.cursor/`)

## Never track

- `.gradle/`, `build/`, `app/build/`, caches, `local.properties`
- `.env`, `scripts/pns_adb_device.env` (keep `.example` stubs)
- Bulk `hfr-runs/` / `perf-runs/` artifacts (unless explicitly intended)
- OS junk: `.DS_Store`, `Thumbs.db`

## Agent commit discipline

1. Review `git status` before every commit
2. Stage **explicit paths** — avoid blind `git add -A`
3. Run `.\scripts\pns_check_repo_hygiene.ps1` before push when hygiene may have drifted
4. Never commit device serials or signing keystores

## Policies

- **No Git LFS** or **submodules** without `[HUMAN]` approval
- Build outputs publish via CI artifacts / GitHub Releases — not git history
